00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.719
Jack: So, let’s have a look at
Scrum Events in a little more

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.890
detail, starting with ‘The Sprint’

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:09.459
Leah: The sprint is a fixed length
event which has a sprint goal.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.520
All events are time-boxed so once
a sprint begins, it is fixed.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.599
The sprint itself, involves a collection
of ‘tasks’ for the team to achieve.

00:00:18.139 --> 00:00:22.220
Each task or ‘user story’ is
allocated a level of complexity

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.450
called a ‘story point’.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:28.949
A sprint project board which is also
known as the ‘Sprint Backlog’ is used

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.330
to track the tasks, and sub-tasks
are positioned in three columns - ‘To

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.510
do’, ‘In progress’, and ‘Done’.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.980
Jack: Sprint planning is the
first meeting of the sprint.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:43.510
It is where achievable items or user
stories, are identified from the product

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:45.730
backlog to be moved to the next sprint.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.560
The team would decide in this meeting,
what can be done within the next

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:53.930
sprint, and then refine the user
stories; for example, they would

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:57.580
determine story-points, how tasks
will get done, the definition of

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.340
done, dependencies, and sub-tasks.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:04.680
The Scrum Master who ensures that
the framework is followed, would

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:09.739
predominately manage this meeting, taking
into consideration priority, capacity,

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.910
and the wider business expectations.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:16.500
However, before this meeting can
take place, the Product Owner would

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:20.180
need to determine the priority
tasks and decide on the sprint goal.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:24.860
Team members would also need to allocate
their own tasks on the product backlog.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.930
Leah: The Daily Scrum, also known as
the ‘Daily Standup’, is a 15 minute

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:33.650
meeting for the internal scrum team,
which is arranged at the same time,

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.190
each working day of the sprint.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:39.900
Its main objective is to determine
progress and update the project board,

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.650
also known as the ‘sprint backlog’, and
adapt the ‘product backlog’ if needed.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:49.850
The focus is on progress and actions, and
self-management is encouraged, as well

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:54.360
as promoting collaboration, improvement,
and transparency amongst team members.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:58.520
It is ‘not’ meant to be a ‘status’
meeting but is meant to be about

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.100
achieving valuable outcomes.

00:02:00.559 --> 00:02:03.560
It is also supposed to eliminate
the need for other meetings,

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:07.649
improve communication and
decision-making, and identify blockers.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:11.890
Jack: The Sprint Review is where the scrum
team present their results from the work

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:16.120
they have done in the current sprint, to
the stakeholders and/or the customers.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:21.570
It is where feedback is given, and
adaptations, alterations, changes and

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:23.099
or improvements can be planned for.

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:27.670
The sprint review is a working session,
not just a presentation and the

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:31.840
product backlog is adjusted to reflect
new information and or feedback.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:34.800
It is usually one of the
last events of the sprint.

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:41.269
Leah: The Sprint Retrospective or retro is
the last meeting and concludes the sprint.

00:02:41.779 --> 00:02:46.310
This is where the team determine what went
well, what could be improved, what needs

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:50.750
greater understanding, and the actions
that need to be taken, moving forward.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:54.560
The retro is a safe place where
the team can come together, give

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:56.350
support and productive feedback.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:00.699
The purpose of the retro is to act on
what has been reviewed, and plan ways

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:02.670
to increase quality and effectiveness.

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:06.230
One of the biggest benefits of
working in Agile is ‘continuous

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:10.589
improvement’, and in Scrum the driver
of improvement is the ‘Retrospective’.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:14.160
Jack: You can hear more about Agile
and Scrum and what it’s like to be

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.019
a Scrum Master in the video below.

